Real bash runs ./r.sh in each new RUN row, but main's scan_gateway_lifecycle
allowed all nine (card t_0a7e8d4a61542b7f, found reviewing PR #2925):

  echo `bash ./r.sh`              echo "`bash ./r.sh`"
  echo `true; bash ./r.sh`        echo ${x:-`bash ./r.sh`}
  echo `true<NL>bash ./r.sh`      echo "$(true; bash ./r.sh)"
  echo "$(true<NL>bash ./r.sh)"   echo "${x:-$(true<NL>bash ./r.sh)}"
  echo ${x:-"$(true<NL>bash ./r.sh)"}

Backtick bodies were never walked for referenced scripts, and a
double-quoted $(…) was a single shlex word, so its commands were never
segments. PR #2859 (cron/lifecycle_guard_substitutions.py) scans every
$(…)/backtick body as its own command text and fixes all nine; this
commit only adds the rows and their python3 ./clean.py twins.

Proof: tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_substitution_bodies.py on main
aea933a8ac: 9 RUN rows failed, 9 twins passed; on #2859 head bbe12dc1b3:
18 passed. Each RUN row asserts the fake hermes marker fired under bash.
---
 ...est_lifecycle_guard_substitution_bodies.py | 42 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 42 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_substitution_bodies.py

diff --git a/tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_substitution_bodies.py b/tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_substitution_bodies.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..24db2a7121e31badc7f37e878dd9dadca13278ee
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_substitution_bodies.py
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+"""Command-substitution bodies are walked for the scripts they run (card t_0a7e8d4a61542b7f).
+
+Found in the review of PR #2925: bash runs ``./r.sh`` in each RUN row, but the guard never read a
+backtick body for referenced scripts, and a double-quoted ``$(…)`` (bare, in a ``${x:-…}``
+default or quoted inside one) was one shlex word, so its ``bash ./r.sh`` command (after a ``;`` or
+a newline) was never a segment. Each row runs under real bash with a fake ``hermes`` that writes a
+marker; each clean twin runs ``python3 ./clean.py`` in the same position and stays allowed.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import pytest
+
+from cron.lifecycle_guard import scan_gateway_lifecycle
+from tests.cron.test_lifecycle_guard_comment_words import _bash_runs, _tree
+
+RUN = [
+    "echo `bash ./r.sh`",
+    'echo "`bash ./r.sh`"',
+    "echo `true; bash ./r.sh`",
+    "echo ${x:-`bash ./r.sh`}",
+    "echo `true\nbash ./r.sh`",
+    'echo "$(true; bash ./r.sh)"',
+    'echo "$(true\nbash ./r.sh)"',
+    'echo "${x:-$(true\nbash ./r.sh)}"',
+    'echo ${x:-"$(true\nbash ./r.sh)"}',
+]
+ALLOWED = [row.replace("bash ./r.sh", "python3 ./clean.py") for row in RUN]
+
+
+@pytest.mark.parametrize("command", RUN)
+def test_script_run_inside_a_command_substitution_is_refused(tmp_path, command):
+    _tree(tmp_path)
+    assert _bash_runs(tmp_path, command), "bash must run the restart, or the row proves nothing"
+    assert scan_gateway_lifecycle(command, cwd=str(tmp_path))[0] is True
+
+
+@pytest.mark.parametrize("command", ALLOWED)
+def test_clean_script_inside_a_command_substitution_stays_allowed(tmp_path, command):
+    _tree(tmp_path)
+    assert not _bash_runs(tmp_path, command)
+    assert scan_gateway_lifecycle(command, cwd=str(tmp_path)) == (False, None)
